    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5daf182a_2e75df98",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T16:02:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is for initrd\u003d\u003dNone case, in this case, the hash descriptors `initrd_debug` or `initrd_normal` are not allowed.\n\nThe check below checks when initrd\u003d\u003dSome, we only allow `initrd_debug` or `initrd_normal`. Basically they are contradictory, how would you like to have them both?",
      "parentUuid": "88ee4852_11e903ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0dfc3624_f0871749",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T10:09:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```\nkernel + initrd_normal + foobar \u003d\u003e failure\nkernel + foobar \u003d\u003e success\n```\nam I missing something?",
      "parentUuid": "5daf182a_2e75df98",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b005e9c_82adc4a5",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T10:16:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I understand here is that\n\nIf initrd \u003d\u003d None:\n- hash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(initrd_normal) \u003d\u003e failure, because we are not expecting any initrd_* descriptor here.\n- hash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(foobar) \u003d\u003e success\n\nIf initrd \u003d\u003d Some:\n- hash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(initrd_normal) \u003d\u003e success\n- hash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(foobar) \u003d\u003e failure\n- hash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(initrd_normal)+ hash_desc(foobar) \u003d\u003e failure. This is what this cl handles, without this cl, the normal verification will pass.\n\nIn vbmeta has non hash descriptor, then it\u0027s failure in both cases.",
      "parentUuid": "0dfc3624_f0871749",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cbc1c7b_8c065da2",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T10:31:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, but I\u0027m asking why do we handle the presence of `foobar` differently depending on initrd\u003d\u003dSome/None. From your own asseessment:\n```\nIf initrd \u003d\u003d None:\nhash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(foobar) \u003d\u003e success\n```\nbut\n```\nIf initrd \u003d\u003d Some:\nhash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(foobar) \u003d\u003e failure\nhash_desc(kernel) + hash_desc(initrd_normal)+ hash_desc(foobar) \u003d\u003e failure\n```\nIt should result in failure in both cases",
      "parentUuid": "3b005e9c_82adc4a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "faeb37cb_d02fdcd6",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T10:32:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you remove the `return Ok(())`, it will handle them the same way.",
      "parentUuid": "9cbc1c7b_8c065da2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5778a7f_03829afe",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T10:34:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Running both checks would be superfluous as `search_initrd_hash_descriptor` checks\n```\npartition_name in (\"initrd_normal\", \"initrd_debug\")\n```\nwhile `search_unexpected_hash_descriptor` checks\n```\npartition_name in (\"kernel\", \"initrd_normal\", \"initrd_debug\")\n```\n\nBut I agree that this could be refactored to merge the 2 paths (TBF, `avb_descriptor_foreach` doesn\u0027t really help with writing clean Rust).\n\n\u003e Basically they are contradictory\n\nA small change that would make this clearer would be to use an `else`, here:\n```\nif payload.initrd.is_some() {\n    verify_vbmeta_has_no_unexpected_descriptor(\n        \u0026vbmeta_images[0],\n        Some(search_unexpected_hash_descriptor),\n    )\n} else {\n    verify_vbmeta_has_no_unexpected_descriptor(\n        \u0026vbmeta_images[0],\n        Some(search_initrd_hash_descriptor),\n    )\n}\n```\nor even\n```\nlet search_func \u003d if payload.initrd.is_some() {\n    Some(search_unexpected_hash_descriptor)\n} else {\n    Some(search_initrd_hash_descriptor)\n};\n\nverify_vbmeta_has_no_unexpected_descriptor(\n    \u0026vbmeta_images[0],\n    search_func,\n)\n```\n\nbut ideally, you\u0027d want these checks to be merged and simply expressed around something like\n```\nlet name \u003d PartitionName::try_from(hash_desc.partition_name()?)?;\n\nif initrd.is_none() \u0026\u0026 matches!(name, PartitionName::InitrdDebug | PartitionName::InitrdNormal) {\n    return Err(AvbSlotVerifyError::InvalidMetadata);\n}\n```\n\nIt would also be nice to be able to distinguish between `InvalidMetadata` originating from libavb and pvmfw itself rejecting the image (at least, through a `log::error!`).",
      "parentUuid": "5daf182a_2e75df98",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ad4024a_64e89f27",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T10:48:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re Pierre:\nI opt an early return instead of `if...else...` because there are more things to do when initrd is some, aosp/2388176 for example.\n\nRe David:\nI thought it was a feature requirement that when initrd is None, we just don\u0027t want to have `initrd_*` descriptors but anything else is okay according to [these comments](https://r.android.com/c/2383895/11). That\u0027s why I did a `for_each(search_**_existence)` here. Instead, if we want\n\n- When initrd \u003d\u003d None, vbmeta should only contain one hash_desc(kernel), all the other cases should fail (that\u0027s what happens after removing `return Ok(()))`.\n\n- When initrd \u003d\u003d Some, vbmeta should contain only hash_desc(kernel) + one or two of [hash_desc(initrd_normal), hash_desc(initrd_debug)].\n\nThen we should do it differently, just collecting the descriptors to check the total number or look if that\u0027s what we want would be better.",
      "parentUuid": "faeb37cb_d02fdcd6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf8382d5_333c3ba6",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T11:40:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, I wanted to agree on how we should handle unexpected partitions before suggesting how to do it better. In general, I just want to make sure that the `no initrd \u003d\u003e no initrd hashdesc` check is independent of `no unknown hashdesc`. We should not enforce `no unknown hashdesc` only in some situations. It needs to be consistent.",
      "parentUuid": "9ad4024a_64e89f27",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "be5fb8d0_4fe91b16",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T11:50:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree. I would prefer to enforce an allowlist here and reject all the unknown desc in both cases, in brief:\n\n- If initrd \u003d\u003d None, allowlist \u003d [kernel]\n- If initrd \u003d\u003d Some, allowlist \u003d [kernel,initrd_normal,initrd_debug]",
      "parentUuid": "bf8382d5_333c3ba6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 586,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 586,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "7929743c14f1de8bfbcc77824efa301fdd17cda0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e47de83_9dcb991e",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 586,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T11:52:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. It would also be nice if the `foreach` could modify that list along the way. That would reject multiple hash descriptors with the same name. You could implement it as a u32 bitmap, for example.",
      "parentUuid": "be5fb8d0_4fe91b16",
